264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (Another feature we launched at the end of 2023 was Malicious Domain Protection. This feature takes a look at the domain string and was built by our labs team, which handles research and development, with the intention of discovering Domain Generation Algorithms \(DGA\), though it finds malicious sites outside of DGAs as well. DGAs are domain strings randomly generated and used in malware attacks, and of increasing importance to block as malware and ransomware continued to grow over the last year.)
/E (Another feature we launched at the end of 2023 was Malicious Domain Protection. This feature takes a look at the domain string and was built by our labs team, which handles research and development, with the intention of discovering Domain Generation Algorithms \(DGA\), though it finds malicious sites outside of DGAs as well. DGAs are domain strings randomly generated and used in malware attacks, and of increasing importance to block as malware and ransomware continued to grow over the last year.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (Looking forward to 2024 at DNSFilter, we will continue to follow the trends and implement changes and additions to our product to adapt to the world around us. We will be launching new filtering capabilities to give our customers tighter controls over the allowed and blocked URLs on their network, among other functionality. )
/E (Looking forward to 2024 at DNSFilter, we will continue to follow the trends and implement changes and additions to our product to adapt to the world around us. We will be launching new filtering capabilities to give our customers tighter controls over the allowed and blocked URLs on their network, among other functionality. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
